  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-09T23:50:38.245Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Now that the depth of field has been added to the camera, this has become a very needed feature. All recent DSLRs and mirrorless cameras have really strong tracking AF with automatic face detection so these cameras do not jump to something random when you go and re-frame your shot, keeping a selected object in focus.\nVRChat inherently knows the location of all the avatar head bones in the instance, so in theory face tracking should be reasonably easy to implement.\nI propose a new \"Tracking\" focus mode that will draw circles over every avatar's head, every circle selectable with the pointer, and upon selection the camera will maintain focus on the selected avatar regardless of its relative position in the frame. The focus should lock if the avatar goes out of frame, and re-focus if the avatar appears in the frame again.",
